{"canonical_source_keys":["fixture:fixture_group_quotient"],"content":"Let G be a group and N a normal subgroup. The quotient map q:G→G/N forgets which representative of a coset was chosen while preserving multiplication: q(xy)=q(x)q(y). A map from G that is constant on cosets factors uniquely through q.","content_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0","contract_version":"mathia-interchange-v1","corpus_origin":"agnostic","corpus_release_id":"mathia-agnostic-representative-v1","derivation_ids":["representative-fixture-authored-for-contract-validation"],"exclusion_reason":null,"licensing_boundary":"repository-authored CC0-compatible fixture","object_id":"mathia_source_8ca37d18443a39cc93ddcc8f7a60a56c8e4a705aaf4c32dac1b1f7749b50e8a8","object_role":"source","parent_ids":[],"quality_state":"accepted","representation_dependencies":[],"source_ids":["fixture_group_quotient"],"source_unit_ids":["fixture_group_quotient"],"span_lineage":[{"line_end":1,"line_start":1,"source_id":"fixture_group_quotient","source_normalized_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0","source_unit_id":"fixture_group_quotient","unit_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0"}],"teacher_provenance":{"kind":"human-authored-fixture","model":null},"training_eligibility":"eligible"}
{"canonical_source_keys":["fixture:fixture_linear_duality"],"content":"For a finite-dimensional vector space V, a linear map T:V→V induces the dual map T*:V*→V* by precomposition. The annihilator of an invariant subspace is invariant under T*, translating a statement about restriction into one about a quotient.","content_sha256":"b57156b7eeea13569e19d4580411c10b12e8284ab80c84aef652b9067ccca8c4","contract_version":"mathia-interchange-v1","corpus_origin":"agnostic","corpus_release_id":"mathia-agnostic-representative-v1","derivation_ids":["representative-fixture-authored-for-contract-validation"],"exclusion_reason":null,"licensing_boundary":"repository-authored CC0-compatible fixture","object_id":"mathia_source_25368c2a2cc0c88ec09df7d7b9adcaff0e9e1a64d271ff2a627e6c225d1d3071","object_role":"source","parent_ids":[],"quality_state":"accepted","representation_dependencies":[],"source_ids":["fixture_linear_duality"],"source_unit_ids":["fixture_linear_duality"],"span_lineage":[{"line_end":1,"line_start":1,"source_id":"fixture_linear_duality","source_normalized_sha256":"b57156b7eeea13569e19d4580411c10b12e8284ab80c84aef652b9067ccca8c4","source_unit_id":"fixture_linear_duality","unit_sha256":"b57156b7eeea13569e19d4580411c10b12e8284ab80c84aef652b9067ccca8c4"}],"teacher_provenance":{"kind":"human-authored-fixture","model":null},"training_eligibility":"eligible"}
{"canonical_source_keys":["fixture:fixture_group_quotient"],"content":"The quotient is not merely a smaller set: it is the universal representation that deliberately discards variation inside each coset while retaining every operation visible to coset-constant maps. Normality is the structural condition that makes the forgotten choice irrelevant to multiplication. If N were not normal, representative dependence would return and the proposed compression would stop being a group quotient.","content_sha256":"c5f63d189bf9f046f7fa58cfdb30be1006c82e88c2da03ff060d3811ff9eee0b","contract_version":"mathia-interchange-v1","corpus_origin":"agnostic","corpus_release_id":"mathia-agnostic-representative-v1","derivation_ids":["representative-fixture-interpretation-v1"],"exclusion_reason":null,"licensing_boundary":"repository-authored CC0-compatible fixture","object_id":"mathia_interpretation_91b108125ff8ded47ac23886068090816e154c0b93ee6557aefe56054123a656","object_role":"interpretation","parent_ids":["mathia_source_8ca37d18443a39cc93ddcc8f7a60a56c8e4a705aaf4c32dac1b1f7749b50e8a8"],"quality_state":"accepted","representation_dependencies":[],"source_ids":["fixture_group_quotient"],"source_unit_ids":["fixture_group_quotient"],"span_lineage":[{"line_end":1,"line_start":1,"source_id":"fixture_group_quotient","source_normalized_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0","source_unit_id":"fixture_group_quotient","unit_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0"}],"teacher_provenance":{"kind":"human-authored-fixture","model":null},"training_eligibility":"eligible"}
{"canonical_source_keys":["fixture:fixture_group_quotient","fixture:fixture_linear_duality"],"content":"Both constructions move a problem to a representation that forgets selected information. The quotient identifies vectors or group elements directly; the annihilator records the same loss contravariantly through functionals. The shared move is controlled forgetting, but the mechanisms are not interchangeable: normality controls multiplication in the group case, whereas finite-dimensional duality controls recovery in the linear case.","content_sha256":"c300dac5a0180937fdb9633bb82e83377a0a5908d885b86f3f36f00178789a4a","contract_version":"mathia-interchange-v1","corpus_origin":"agnostic","corpus_release_id":"mathia-agnostic-representative-v1","derivation_ids":["representative-fixture-synthesis-v1"],"exclusion_reason":null,"licensing_boundary":"repository-authored CC0-compatible fixture","object_id":"mathia_synthesis_ae16b96639588a4fb2f4178bfd611762a0059376c1bd2f89678fe895bc35a9f6","object_role":"synthesis","parent_ids":["mathia_source_8ca37d18443a39cc93ddcc8f7a60a56c8e4a705aaf4c32dac1b1f7749b50e8a8","mathia_source_25368c2a2cc0c88ec09df7d7b9adcaff0e9e1a64d271ff2a627e6c225d1d3071"],"quality_state":"accepted","representation_dependencies":[],"source_ids":["fixture_group_quotient","fixture_linear_duality"],"source_unit_ids":["fixture_group_quotient","fixture_linear_duality"],"span_lineage":[{"line_end":1,"line_start":1,"source_id":"fixture_group_quotient","source_normalized_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0","source_unit_id":"fixture_group_quotient","unit_sha256":"872f9531436467b8f406fd0309d011876acd67840b32aa6bee50579c1f5209e0"},{"line_end":1,"line_start":1,"source_id":"fixture_linear_duality","source_normalized_sha256":"b57156b7eeea13569e19d4580411c10b12e8284ab80c84aef652b9067ccca8c4","source_unit_id":"fixture_linear_duality","unit_sha256":"b57156b7eeea13569e19d4580411c10b12e8284ab80c84aef652b9067ccca8c4"}],"teacher_provenance":{"